"id":"s24","label":"Ch. 5"},{"id":"s25","label":"Ch. 6","title":"June 18th.—The misery of self-reproach which I suffered yesterday"},{"id":"s26","label":"Ch. 7","title":"June 19th.—The events of yesterday warned me to be ready, sooner or"},{"id":"s27","label":"Ch. 8","title":"June 19th.—I had only got as far as the top of the stairs when the"},{"id":"s28","label":"Ch. 9"},{"id":"s29","label":"Ch. 10"},{"id":"s30","label":"Ch. 1","title":"I am asked to state plainly what I know of the progress of Miss"},{"id":"s31","label":"Ch. 2"},{"id":"s32","label":"Ch. 1","title":"THE NARRATIVE OF HESTER PINHORN, COOK IN THE SERVICE OF COUNT FOSCO"},{"id":"s33","label":"Ch. 5","title":"THE NARRATIVE OF WALTER HARTRIGHT"},{"id":"s34","label":"Ch. 1"},{"id":"s35","label":"Ch. 2"},{"id":"s36","label":"Ch. 3"},{"id":"s37","label":"Ch. 4","title":"No circumstance of the slightest importance happened on my way to the"},{"id":"s38","label":"Ch. 5"},{"id":"s39","label":"Ch. 6","title":"The address communicated by Mrs. Todd took me to a lodging-house"},{"id":"s40","label":"Ch. 7"},{"id":"s41","label":"Ch. 8"},{"id":"s42","label":"Ch. 9","title":"I left the house, feeling that Mrs. Catherick had helped me a step"},{"id":"s43","label":"Ch. 10"},{"id":"s44","label":"Ch. 11","title":"The inquest was hurried for certain local reasons which weighed with"},{"id":"s45","label":"Ch. 1","title":"My first impulse, after reading Mrs. Catherick’s extraordinary"},{"id":"s46","label":"Ch. 2"},{"id":"s47","label":"Ch. 3"},{"id":"s48","label":"Ch. 4","title":"The course of this narrative, steadily flowing on, bears me away from"},{"id":"s49","label":"Ch. 5"},{"id":"s50","label":"Ch. 6","title":"My first conviction as soon as I found myself outside the house, was"},{"id":"s51","label":"Ch. 7","title":"There was no lamp in the hall, but by the dim light of the kitchen"},{"id":"s52","label":"Ch. 1","title":"When I closed the last leaf of the Count’s manuscript the half-hour"},{"id":"s53","label":"Ch. 2","title":"Two more events remain to be added to the chain before it reaches"},{"id":"s54","label":"Ch. 3"}],"groups":[{"id":"g-glyde","label":"Glyde (shared surname)"},{"id":"g-fairlie","label":"Fairlie (shared surname)"},{"id":"g-fosco","label":"Fosco (shared surname)"},{"id":"g-rubelle","label":"Rubelle (shared surname)"}],"characters":[{"id":"marian-halcombe","name":"Marian Halcombe","aliases":["Miss Halcombe","Marian"],"role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “My name is Marian Halcombe; and I am as inaccurate as women usually are, in calling Mr.”"},{"id":"percival-glyde","name":"Percival Glyde","aliases":["Sir Percival","Sir Percival Glyde"],"role":"protagonist","group":"g-glyde","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: ““Sir Percival Glyde.””"},{"id":"laura-fairlie","name":"Laura Fairlie","aliases":["Laura"],"role":"protagonist","group":"g-fairlie","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: “The water-colour drawing that I made of Laura Fairlie, at an after period, in the place and attitude in which I first saw her, lies on my desk while I write.”"},{"id":"anne-catherick","name":"Anne Catherick","aliases":["Mrs. Catherick","Anne"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: “This sister comes all the way from Hampshire—her name is Mrs.”"},{"id":"count","name":"Count","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s17","summary":"First mention: “But when her marriage took place, somewhat late in life, and when that marriage united her to an Italian gentleman named Fosco, or, rather, to an Italian nobleman—seeing that he rejoiced in the title of Count—Mr.”"},{"id":"lady-glyde","name":"Lady Glyde","aliases":["Glyde"],"role":"major","group":"g-glyde","firstAppearance":"s17","summary":"First mention: “If Lady Glyde died without leaving children, her half-sister Miss Halcombe, and any other relatives or friends whom she might be anxious to benefit, would, on her husband’s death, divide among them such shares of her…”"},{"id":"mr-fairlie","name":"Mr. Fairlie","role":"major","group":"g-fairlie","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “The references were to be sent to Mr.”"},{"id":"walter-hartright","name":"Walter Hartright","aliases":["Mr. Hartright","Hartright"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Was I Walter Hartright?”"},{"id":"miss-fairlie","name":"Miss Fairlie","role":"supporting","group":"g-fairlie","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Fairlie my uncle, and Miss Fairlie my sister.”"},{"id":"mrs-clements","name":"Mrs. Clements","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: “It was very late, but there was a girl up at needle-work in the house, and she helped me to rouse Mrs.”"},{"id":"percival","name":"Percival","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s16","summary":"First mention: “If Sir Percival would consent to spare her for the present, she would undertake to give him his final answer before the end of the year.”"},{"id":"count-fosco","name":"Count Fosco","role":"supporting","group":"g-fosco","firstAppearance":"s17","summary":"First mention: “Count Fosco, though not a rich man, was not a penniless adventurer either.”"},{"id":"pesca","name":"Pesca","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Without being actually a dwarf—for he was perfectly well proportioned from head to foot—Pesca was, I think, the smallest human being I ever saw out of a show-room.”"},{"id":"madame-fosco","name":"Madame Fosco","role":"supporting","group":"g-fosco","firstAppearance":"s17","summary":"First mention: “Considering the relative ages of the two ladies, the aunt’s chance, in the ordinary course of nature, of receiving the ten thousand pounds, was thus rendered doubtful in the extreme; and Madame Fosco resented her brot…”"},{"id":"mr-gilmore","name":"Mr. Gilmore","aliases":["Gilmore"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “He has written to London, to the family solicitor, Mr.”"},{"id":"walter","name":"Walter","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““I don’t know what would have happened, Walter,” said my mother, “if you had delayed much longer.”"},{"id":"mr-dawson","name":"Mr. Dawson","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s30","summary":"First mention: “He despatched a groom, on horseback, for the nearest medical man, Mr.”"},{"id":"mrs-rubelle","name":"Mrs. Rubelle","role":"supporting","group":"g-rubelle","firstAppearance":"s30","summary":"First mention: “I was instructed that this person’s name was Mrs.”"},{"id":"mr-kyrle","name":"Mr. Kyrle","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s23","summary":"First mention: “Gilmore’s partner, Mr.”"},{"id":"mrs-vesey","name":"Mrs. Vesey","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “My sister is in her own room, nursing that essentially feminine malady, a slight headache; and her old governess, Mrs.”"},{"id":"louis","name":"Louis","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s6","summary":"First mention: ““Louis,” said Mr.”"},{"id":"mrs-fairlie","name":"Mrs. Fairlie","role":"minor","group":"g-fairlie","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Mrs.”"},{"id":"mrs-michelson","name":"Mrs. Michelson","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s24","summary":"First mention: ““Mrs.”"},{"id":"countess","name":"Countess","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s21","summary":"First mention: “I will dispose of the Countess first, so as to have done with the woman as soon as possible.”"},{"id":"fanny","name":"Fanny","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s26","summary":"First mention: “But my lady ran upstairs to her own room in tears, and Sir Percival has ordered me to give Fanny warning to leave in an hour’s time.””"},{"id":"st-john-s-wood","name":"St. John’s Wood","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““Yes,” I replied, “that is the way: it leads to St.”"},{"id":"mr-merriman","name":"Mr. Merriman","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s17","summary":"First mention: “Just as it had fluttered to the ground, there was a knock at my door, and Sir Percival’s solicitor, Mr.”"},{"id":"mrs-todd","name":"Mrs. Todd","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: ““Mrs.”"},{"id":"englishman","name":"Englishman","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “The ruling idea of his life appeared to be, that he was bound to show his gratitude to the country which had afforded him an asylum and a means of subsistence by doing his utmost to turn himself into an Englishman.”"},{"id":"mr-goodricke","name":"Mr. Goodricke","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s32","summary":"First mention: “Mr.”"},{"id":"madame-rubelle","name":"Madame Rubelle","role":"minor","group":"g-rubelle","firstAppearance":"s51","summary":"First mention: “Confidential persons were semi-officially connected with me, whose exertions I was authorised to direct, Monsieur and Madame Rubelle being among the number.”"},{"id":"mr-wansborough","name":"Mr. Wansborough","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s42","summary":"First mention: “Mr.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"englishman","target":"pesca","weight":4,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 2."}]},{"id":"r2","source":"pesca","target":"walter","weight":13,"phases":[{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":7,"note":"First named together in Ch. 3."},{"at":"s53","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":12}]},{"id":"r3","source":"mr-fairlie","target":"pesca","weight":6,"phases":[{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":5,"note":"First named together in Ch. 3."}]},{"id":"r4","source":"mrs-vesey","target":"walter-hartright","weight":15,"phases":[{"at":"s5","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":2,"note":"First named together in Ch. 6."},{"at":"s14","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":12}]},{"id":"r5","source":"mr-fair